{"qid":"Q403","names":["Serbia"],"title":"Serbia","endonym":{"native":"Србија","lang":"sr"},"capsule":"The modern Serbian state emerged from the dissolution of Austria-Hungary and the Armistice of 1918, when Serbia became the founding component of the Kingdom of Serbs, Croats and Slovenes (later Yugoslavia). After successive Yugoslav arrangements — the royal dictatorship of 1929, the communist federation from 1945, and the looser federation from 1974 — Slovenia and Croatia declared independence in 1991, triggering the Yugoslav Wars; Serbia and Montenegro formed a rump Federal Republic of Yugoslavia in 1992 and later the State Union of Serbia and Montenegro in 2003. Montenegro voted for independence in May 2006, leaving Serbia as a fully independent republic from June 2006; the 2008 unilateral declaration of independence by Kosovo, administered by the UN since 1999, remains a major unresolved territorial and legal dispute. Serbia applied for EU membership in 2009 and received candidate status in 2012.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Serbia's internationally recognised borders are precisely defined by post-Yugoslav treaties, with the sole substantive dispute being Kosovo's status; the historical period from 1918 onward is exceptionally well-documented.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Serbia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serbia"},{"label":"Britannica: Serbia","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Serbia"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Serbia and Montenegro","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serbia_and_Montenegro"},{"label":"Wikipedia: 2008 Kosovo declaration of independence","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2008_Kosovo_declaration_of_independence"}],"britannica":"place/Serbia","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Serbia and Montenegro","rulers":[{"qid":"Q483290","name":"Boris Tadić","start":2004,"end":2012,"image":"Boris Tadić (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Boris%20Tadi%C4%87%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY 4.0","artist":"European Commission","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"Борис Тадић","nativeLang":"sr"},{"qid":"Q33031","name":"Vojislav Koštunica","start":2004,"end":2008,"image":"Flickr - europeanpeoplesparty - EPP Congress Rome 2006 (68) (cropped 2).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Flickr%20-%20europeanpeoplesparty%20-%20EPP%20Congress%20Rome%202006%20(68)%20(cropped%202).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY 2.0","artist":"European People's Party","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"Војислав Коштуница","nativeLang":"sr"},{"qid":"Q204723","name":"Mirko Cvetković","start":2008,"end":2012,"image":"Mirko Cvetković.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mirko%20Cvetkovi%C4%87.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","artist":"Democratic Party","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"Мирко Цветковић","nativeLang":"sr"},{"qid":"Q57431","name":"Tomislav Nikolić","start":2012,"end":2017,"image":"Tomislav Nikolić, official portrait.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Tomislav%20Nikoli%C4%87%2C%20official%20portrait.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","artist":"General Secretariat of the President of the Republic of Serbia","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"Томислав Николић","nativeLang":"sr"},{"qid":"Q1192059","name":"Slavica Đukić Dejanović","start":2012,"end":2012,"image":"Slavica Đukić Dejanović.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Slavica%20%C4%90uki%C4%87%20Dejanovi%C4%87.jpg?width